      "html": "<ul><li>Synonym: Arius verrucosus</li><li>IUCN Red List: Not Evaluated</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/hemiarius_verrucosus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Asia: middle and lower Mekong River basin. Type locality: Laos, Champasak, Mekong River at Ban Hang Khone, just downstream from Khone Falls.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/hemiarius_verrucosus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Inhabits lower reaches of rivers and estuaries and feeds on fishes and shellfishes.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/hemiarius_verrucosus.htm",
      "html": "<p>In most, if not all species, the male carries the relatively large eggs in its mouth until hatching.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/hemiarius_verrucosus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: The specific name verrucosus means warty, referring to numerous small bumps on the pectoral spines and dorsal surface of the neurocranium.</p><p>Described by Ng, 2003.</p>"
    }
